Aerie-Purpose: Remove the Helium services app menu item, its menu icon nag, the download bubble link and summary for disabled extension downloads, and the status string that named Helium services on chrome://components.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/ui/toolbar (app_menu_model, app_menu_icon_controller), chrome/browser/ui/browser_command_controller.cc, chrome/browser/ui/chrome_pages, chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings/chrome/browser/download (download_commands and the models), chrome/browser/ui/download/download_bubble_security_view_info.cc, chrome/app (generated_resources.grd, chromium_strings.grd, chrome_command_ids.h)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #94. Issue #23 (services/0006) removed the Helium services settings page, but Helium's
services-schema-nag.patch still put "Review Helium services updates" in the app menu (command
IDC_HELIUM_SERVICES_OPEN, ShowHeliumServices, and a "Services updated" label and tooltip on the menu
button that follow a pref), and add-copy-download-link-context-menu.patch gave the download bubble an
OPEN_HELIUM_SERVICES button that opened the page that is gone. This patch removes them: the menu
item, the command, the icon type and its two strings, the download command and every switch case
for it, and the grd messages IDS_HELIUM_SERVICES_SCHEMA_MENU_ITEM, IDS_APP_MENU_BUTTON_HELIUM_SERVICES_UPDATE,
IDS_APPMENU_TOOLTIP_HELIUM_SERVICES_UPDATE, IDS_DOWNLOAD_BUBBLE_INTERRUPTED_SUBPAGE_SUMMARY_HELIUM_SERVICES_DISABLED
and IDS_COMPONENTS_SVC_STATUS_ERROR_HELIUM_SERVICES (services/0007 already stopped using the last one).
The bubble keeps a summary for an extension download that was blocked, now without a button and in
Aerie words (IDS_AERIE_DOWNLOAD_BUBBLE_EXTENSION_DOWNLOADS_OFF, chrome/app/aerie_services_strings.grdp;
chrome/browser/aerie_download/download_bubble_summary_browsertest.cc guards it). The enum value 24 of
DownloadCommands is left unused, with a comment, so the numbers of the others do not change; Helium
never added it to tools/metrics/histograms/metadata/download/enums.xml, so there is no entry to remove.

Helium text that stays in the source and cannot reach a user (checked for #94):
- The services changelog in components/helium_services/schema.cc ("you'll be notified about major changes
  to Helium services ..."), which web-push-service.patch carries as context. Its only reader is
  HeliumServicesSchemaHandler, which answers the settings page messages getServicesSchemaChangelog and
  updateServicesSchemaVersion. The only page that sent them was the services page, which services/0006
  removed together with changelog_proxy.ts (no remaining file under chrome/browser/resources names either
  message). The handler stays registered in settings_ui.cc, because later Aerie settings patches use that
  line as context, but nothing sends it a message. ShouldShowSchemaNotification now has no other caller
  (the menu item and the icon nag were the others).
- The settings strings for the schema notice and for web push (IDS_SETTINGS_HELIUM_SCHEMA_*,
  IDS_SETTINGS_HELIUM_SERVICES_WEB_PUSH*, IDS_SETTINGS_HELIUM_SERVICES_PUSH_SERVER_*, ..._UPDATE) are
  load-time data for the removed services page. No element of any remaining page reads them.
- The web push service (kHeliumWebPush) is a feature that is off by default, and nothing in Aerie turns it on.
  Its "Helium services." text in web-push-service.patch is the description field of a network traffic
  annotation. It is read by Chromium's annotation audit, not shown by any page. Line 115 of that patch is
  a TODO comment.
The schema component (components/helium_services/schema.*) and its pref stay, as Helium's other plumbing
does, to keep Helium bumps cheap. tests/test_helium_services_ui_removed.py checks that no marker is left.
The Bench check branding_no_helium forces a failed download and a failed component update and reads the
download bubble and chrome://components.

Depends on the Helium patches services-schema-nag.patch, add-copy-download-link-context-menu.patch,
add-specific-error-for-disabled-extension-downloads.patch, services-prefs.patch and component-updates.patch,
on services/0006 (it edits the same lines of chrome_pages.cc and download_ui_model.cc) and on
services/0007.

